# The Vercel project root is the repo root (see api/index.py for why), so trim
# it to what the edge gateway actually imports: `edge/`, the parts of `server/`
# behind the shared login template, and brand.config.json.
#
# The SPA is deliberately excluded — it is served by the Databricks App, and the
# edge only proxies to it.
frontend/
node_modules/
.git/
docs/
tests/
scripts/
resources/
.databricks/
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# `vercel build` run locally writes api/pyproject.toml + api/uv.lock from the
# local uv config. On this machine that pins an internal Databricks package
# proxy, and once uploaded it takes precedence over api/requirements.txt — the
# remote build then hangs fetching from a host it cannot reach. Keep resolution
# on requirements.txt by never shipping these.
api/pyproject.toml
api/uv.lock
uv.lock
.python-version
